      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for acute pain or inflammation in the hospital setting.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours**, the usual dose for analgesia.\n- **1600 mg per day in total**, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me the dose you intended, or confirm that 1600 mg four times daily is deliberate. If it is, I'd suggest checking with pharmacy or the prescriber first. I'll enter the order as soon as you confirm."
